+## Dossier Review
+
+Peter owns Benchmark's [dossiers](data-model.md#dossiers-and-review-evidence) and reviews proposed answers to their explicit unknowns. Use the operator-supplied document for each authorized client. Keep a **Dossiers** tab in the existing review spreadsheet with **Client** and **Dossier** columns, one row per client and a link to its document. Add dossiers as Vikas supplies them; preserve the article review tab.
+
+Propose supported answers in the dossier through **Suggesting mode**, so Peter can accept or reject the wording. Include a source comment identifying the unknown, explaining the answer in natural language that sounds like Vikas, and linking directly to the supporting source. Identify the exact dossier phrase in the comment so Peter can find it even if the comment is not visibly attached to the text. Preserve useful wording and qualifications around the answer. Use comments to support suggested answers; factual-conflict comments are a separate, deferred operation under [Product](product.md#purpose-and-scope).
+
+Leave unanswered items explicit in the assessment for Vikas when research cannot establish an answer, including what Peter or the client must confirm. Do not add comments that merely repeat existing requests for confirmation. Peter's acceptance, rejection or reply determines his disposition of a suggestion; report that separately from whether the evidence supports it. Do not accept, reject or resolve review items on Peter's behalf. [Architecture](architecture.md#dossier-research-and-review) defines the research and posting flow; [Engineering](engineering.md#dossier-review-verification) defines completion evidence.
